r came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them, more than any other pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 5 grids. In 2025 that middle swung from 186% of normal in May to June down to 37% in November to December. So far in 2026 every published pair has come in under 90%, with March to April at 73%. Grid 23008 had its driest year in 1991 at 68%.</p>"}
